			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">I have to pick the Packers-Patriots Super Bowl because they're my two favourite teams <img src="images/smiles/smile.gif" alt="Smile" border="0" />
<br />

<br />
If you want a more unbiased opinion, new England is still by far the best team in the NFL. And as great as Philly looks right now, McNabb still has to prove to me that he won't choke in a big game, so I'm hesitant to pick Philly. I'm also hesitant to say Minnesota, because their defense is suspect, although they have the best offensive potential in the NFL.
<br />

<br />
And the Packers can easily still make the playoffs provided their defense plays at least mediocre. They have their 2 division games against the Vikes, 1 against Philly, and 1 against St. Louis, and then 5 easy games. Pretty leniant schedule. And take into account that the Vikings <span style="font-style: italic">always</span> have a much worse second half than first half, and I think Green Bay's chanes are looking up <img src="images/smiles/nod.gif" alt="Nod" border="0" /> Just let Brett throw the ball, which they didn't do early this season except for the Indy game.</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
